  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 accuracy, showing that multiprofile + avgpool is a highly effective combination. The image-only baseline (resnet50) was very weak (0.208), and scgpt single-profile (0.411) underperformed pca_n2000 single-profile (0.485), suggesting encoder choice matters. scvi_n200 is the only RNA encoder not yet tested in any setting. Config_005 isolates the encoder variable by swapping pca_n2000 → scvi_n200 while keeping the proven-best multiprofile + avgpool configuration. This tells us whether a learned latent encoder (scvi) can surpass a linear PCA projection in the multiprofile regime, which directly informs whether further encoder exploration is worthwhile or whether we should pivot to multimodal fusion with the best encoder. With 4 experiments remaining after this one, establishing the best RNA backbone before testing multimodal combinations is the highest-information use of this slot."
}

